  {
    "unit_id": "u0052",
    "excerpt": "This is a work-in-progress FOSS implementation focused on the most widely used open 3D formats.\nSeveral members exist on the public API surface but throw `NotImplementedException` in this\nedition, including: Draco decode/encode (`DracoFormat`), PDF scene extraction (`PdfFormat`), PLY\nencoding (`PlyFormat.Encode` — PLY is import-only), Microsoft 3MF buildable/object-type accessors,\nRVM attribute loading, ZIP-backed file systems, NURBS curve evaluation, mesh boolean/triangulate\noperations on `PolygonModifier`, and text-watermark encode/decode. License and trial-management\nAPIs (`License`, `Metered`) are intentionally not implemented, since they don't apply to an\nopen-source project. Rendering (`Scene.Render`) is also not implemented in this edition.",
    "classification": "2_mechanism_explanation",
    "disposition": "corrected",
    "target_section": "Scope and Limitations",
    "verification": {
      "status": "verified_against_source",
      "evidence_type": "clone_cache_path",
      "evidence_ref": "src/main/Aspose.ThreeD/Aspose/ThreeD/Formats/IOService.cs"
    },
    "correction_reason": "Old README's PLY-encoding claim (PlyFormat.Encode, 'import-only') is itself inaccurate for the real Scene.Save/Open dispatch path -- PlyReader/PlyWriter (registered in IOService.CreateImporter/CreateExporter) provide real, working PLY import AND export; only the confusable, non-dispatched Formats.PlyFormat.Encode/Decode decoy throws. Executable proof: reports/plan_state/readme-disposition-remediation-2026-08-18/evidence/3d-net-ply-proof/ (dotnet run output, 2026-08-19). All other format claims in this unit (Draco, PDF, 3MF buildable metadata, RVM attributes) independently re-verified true -- no dispatcher/reader/writer exists for Draco or PDF anywhere in the codebase.",
    "ledger_migration_note": "2026-09-02 field migration: correction text moved from excluded_reason (pre-fix gate workaround) to correction_reason; disposition/verification untouched"
  },
